{"title":"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<div style=\"text-align:center\">\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2007_CyMO-25.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/20/2007_CyMO-25.PNG/500px-2007_CyMO-25.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"500\" height=\"188\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/20/2007_CyMO-25.PNG/750px-2007_CyMO-25.PNG 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/2/20/2007_CyMO-25.PNG 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p>A jeweller makes crosses, according to the pattern shown above. The crosses are made from golden cyclical <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">discs</a>, with <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Diameter\" title=\"Diameter\">diameter</a> of 1cm each. The height of a cross, which is made from 402 such discs is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/1/de1390e21094bf65c8181a3f4500fd4f88077262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } 198cm\\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } 2m\\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } 201cm\\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } 202cm\\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } 204cm$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"526\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> represents the number of the cross, then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af39e8f48d02497aae57a6d4ab14e6187b859423.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4n + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> disks in the cross (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/1/b417a127620d5b467fe7a48ad5f7d843e5c390b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> to count for the 4 legs of the cross, plus one for the center and one for the bottom leg). So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/a/f6a9783e8756d0b4de02f12ce52d5431b6983852.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle 4n+2=402 \\Rightarrow n = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"193\" height=\"14\" />. The number of discs from top to bottom is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/3/d63c715e01b7cdbe1b53658161e325fb52f46972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n + 2 = 202 \\Longrightarrow \\mathrm{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"155\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; align:center; width:60%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum\" title=\"2007 Cyprus MO/Lyceum\">2007 Cyprus MO, Lyceum</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problems\" title=